                  "It is commenced by filing (delivering to the clerk in the county of suit) the summons and complaint with the CCA 1911 fee; that filing date is the commencement for CPLR 203 (NY:CPLR-203-accrual-interposition). The clerk date-stamps and returns a copy. Jurisdiction over the defendant is acquired only by serving it with the summons and complaint. The actual index number must appear on the summons as served; an omission is cured by stipulation or by leave of court, which is not unreasonably withheld.",
